READING. The welds are the same 6 bonds at every wood, because the
construction always closes to one molecule. Removing them is what the
last column shows: the condensed linkage the model forms BY CHOICE, against
the measured value. If that column is near zero while 'model-ref' is not,
the model's condensed excess is the single-molecule constraint, not the fit.

